        "notes": "Typical color range: 12-176 EBC (typical 23)\n\nPrickly Pear, a fruit native to the Americas, has found its way into the world of beer brewing. Known for its vibrant pink color and unique flavor profile, Prickly Pear adds a refreshing and slightly sweet taste to beers. Its influence on the taste of beer can range from subtle undertones to more pronounced fruity notes depending on how it is used in the brewing process.\n\nPrickly Pear is primarily used as an adjunct ingredient in beer brewing. It can be added during fermentation or incorporated into the mash to extract its flavors and colors. Additionally, it is often utilized alongside other fruits such as citrus or berries to create complex and well-balanced brews.\n\nApart from enhancing flavor, Prickly Pear also brings some notable properties to beer brewing. The fruit contains high levels of antioxidants which can contribute to preserving freshness in beers over time. Furthermore, Prickly Pears are rich in essential vitamins and minerals that can add nutritional value to brewed beverages.\n\nWhile there are no specific styles exclusively brewed with Prickly Pear, it pairs exceptionally well with lighter-bodied beers such as wheat ales or lagers due to its delicate sweetness and aroma presence. These styles allow the flavors of Prickly Pear shine through without overpowering other elements present in the beer."
