        "notes": "Also known as: Rolled Oats\n\nBeer Analytics subtype: Unmalted Adjunct\n\nTypical color range: 1-4 EBC (typical 4)\n\nFlaked Oats are commonly used in beer brewing as an unmalted adjunct. They contribute a light color to the beer and are known for their ability to enhance the body and mouthfeel. Due to their high protein content, flaked oats create a smooth and silky texture in the finished product. Flaked Oats are often included in beer styles such as stouts, porters, and hazy IPAs . These styles benefit from the addition of flaked oats as they help create a creamy and full-bodied mouthfeel. The flavor profile of flaked oats is relatively neutral, allowing other ingredients to shine, while also adding a subtle sweetness and enhancing the overall balance of the beer."
