        "notes": "Also known as: GLH-8732\n\nFlavor notes: Bubblegum, Cinnamon, Grapes, Juicy, Melon, Peach, Watermelon\n\nOriginating from the United States of America, this dual-purpose hop is known for its delightful aroma and flavor profile. Emerald Spire imparts a fruit-forward and delicious character to the beer. Its aroma profile is rich with notes of peach, juicy fruit, white grape, watermelon, bubble gum, and melon rind. Brewers have also identified additional aromas such as Smarties, Fruity Pebbles, cinnamon, nutty undertones, very ripe peach, fruit punch, and honeydew. What sets Emerald Spire apart is its unique finish: it boasts excellent white grape notes and concludes with a champagne-like dryness. This distinct characteristic has made it an invaluable tool for brewers looking to craft a novel flavor profile in their beers."
