          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 3.5
          }
        },
        "substitutes": "Crystal, Hallertauer Mittelfrüh, Mount Hood",
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Citrus, Floral, Herbal, Lemon, Noble, Rose, Spicy, Tea, Woody\n\nLiberty hops are a popular choice among homebrewers for their delicate and versatile characteristics. This hop variety originated in the United States in the 1980s as a result of a breeding program that aimed to create a domestic alternative to the noble Hallertau Mittelfrüh hops from Germany. Liberty hops are a product of a cross between the Hallertau Mittelfrüh and a disease resistant German aroma male. This gives Liberty hops a unique flavor profile that combines the noble hop characteristics with increased resistance to diseases and pests, making it an excellent choice for homebrewers seeking a reliable and flavorful hop.\n\nThe flavor profile of Liberty hops is characterized by its mild floral and spicy notes, with a touch of citrus and a subtle earthiness. This balanced profile lends itself well to a wide variety of beer styles, particularly those that benefit from a delicate hop presence, such as lagers, pilsners, and light ales. The alpha acid content of Liberty hops typically ranges from 3-5%, making them a popular choice for both aroma and bittering applications in brewing. When used in the brewing process, Liberty hops can impart a refined bitterness that does not overwhelm the palate, allowing for the delicate flavors of the malt and other ingredients to shine through. As a homebrewer, experimenting with Liberty hops in your recipes can result in sophisticated, well-rounded brews that showcase a delightful balance of flavors."
      },
      {
        "name": "Limonadier",
        "hop_type": "aroma",
        "origin": "Canada",
        "folder_path": "Canada",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
