            "unit": "%",
            "value": 11.0
          }
        },
        "substitutes": "Cascade, Centennial, Citra",
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Citrus, Fruity, Grapefruit, Lemon, Mango, Pine, Zesty\n\nLimonadier hops are a testament to the innovative spirit of the craft brewing movement, particularly emerging from the fertile grounds of Quebec. Originating from the Double LL farm in St-Édouard-de-Lotbinière, these hops are a proud product of Canadian agriculture, boasting a lineage that includes the popular Cascade variety. As a dual-purpose hop, Limonadier is versatile in the brewing process, suitable for both bittering and aroma additions in a variety of beer styles such as Pale Ale, IPA, Saison, and Trappist.\n\nThe flavor profile of Limonadier is distinctively citrus-forward, with a pronounced lemon character that inspired its name. This lemon essence is complemented by notes of grapefruit, adding a zesty complexity to the hop's profile. Beyond the citrus realm, Limonadier surprises with a peculiar blend of very ripe mango and resinous pine, creating a \"fruit bomb\" sensation that can elevate the sensory experience of any brew."
      },
      {
        "name": "Lotus",
        "hop_type": "aroma",
        "origin": "United States",
        "folder_path": "United States",
        "alpha_acid": {
