            "unit": "%",
            "value": 6.0
          }
        },
        "notes": "Also known as: ID-158\n\nFlavor notes: Apple, Citrus, Floral, Honey, Melon, Pine, Stone Fruit, Strawberry, Tropical Fruits, Vanilla\n\nPink Hops, also known as Experimental ID-158, is a promising new hop variety developed by Jackson Farms in Wilder, Idaho—the same innovators behind the popular Idaho 7 hops. First commercially available in 2022, this variety earned its nickname from the Pink flags that marked the test fields during its development. It quickly caught the attention of brewers for its uniquely layered flavor profile and versatility, particularly in hop-forward styles like Hazy IPAs and Pale Ales.\n\nWhat sets Pink Hops apart is its vibrant mix of bright citrus and juicy stone fruit flavors, combined with more nuanced notes like honey, apple, melon, strawberry, and a subtle touch of vanilla. The result is a hop that brings complexity and balance, lending both aromatic punch and soft fruity sweetness. This makes it a great choice for hazy and sessionable styles where hop flavor takes center stage but bitterness is dialed back. The 2023 crop, in particular, stood out for its expressive aroma and flavor intensity, making Pink Hops a standout choice for adventurous homebrewers looking to experiment with something fresh and exciting."
      },
