        "notes": "Svalöf Mauritz is a hop variety originating from Sweden. Developed at Svalöf in the 1930s, this hop has a rich history and is now grown on a small scale, with manual harvesting carried out by Föreningen Humlebygget at Humletorkan in Näsum. As an aroma hop, Svalöf Mauritz is known for its low alpha acid content, typically around 3%. Given its aromatic properties, it can impart distinct flavors and aromas to the brew, making it a favorite among homebrewers looking to experiment with unique hop profiles."
