          }
        },
        "notes": "Also known as: N1/69\n\nFlavor notes: Citrus, Grassy, Mango, Pineapple, Plum, Pungent, Resinous, Spicy, Woody\n\nSouthern Sublime is a unique hop variety that originates from South Africa. This hop is known for its high alpha content and is daylight neutral. Its genetic lineage can be traced back to a diploid seedling that was selected from a cross between the Nugget hop and 89J1/101. This South African-bred hop is particularly notable for its distinct aroma profile, which boasts a combination of pungent, Kool-Aid, juicy fruit, pineapple, citrus, mango, red plums, grassy, spicy, woody, and resin notes. Such a diverse and intense aroma makes it a perfect choice for brewing hop-forward beers, especially the West Coast-style IPAs ."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sovereign",
        "hop_type": "bittering",
        "origin": "Great Britain",
        "folder_path": "Great Britain",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
