          }
        },
        "substitutes": "Chinook, Columbus, Galena, Magnum",
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Citrus, Earthy, Floral, Geranium, Ginger, Herbal, Lychee, Pineapple, Resinous, Stone Fruit, Tropical Fruits, Woody\n\nNugget hops have been a staple in the brewing industry since their introduction in the early 1980s. Developed by the USDA Breeding Program in Oregon, this hop variety is a cross between the Brewer's Gold and a high alpha-acid male hop. Nugget hops quickly gained popularity due to their impressive dual-purpose profile, offering both high alpha acids and an appealing aroma. With a robust and well-rounded character, these hops are perfect for brewing various beer styles, such as American Ales, IPAs, Stouts, and Barleywines.\n\nThe flavor profile of Nugget hops is characterized by its earthy, herbal, and slightly spicy notes, which add a delightful complexity to your homebrews. Boasting an alpha acid content typically ranging from 12-14%, Nugget hops contribute a firm and clean bitterness to the beer. The moderate aroma profile, on the other hand, showcases subtle hints of wood, pine, and floral qualities, which can add a touch of finesse to your creations. Given their versatility, Nugget hops can be used throughout the brewing process, from bittering to late-addition aroma hopping, making them an excellent option for both single-hop and multi-hop recipes. Whether you're brewing a hop-forward IPA or a more balanced American Ale, Nugget hops will undoubtedly provide an exceptional foundation for your next homebrew project."
      },
      {
