        "notes": "Flavor notes: Aromatic, Bubblegum, Cedar, Earthy, Herbal, Pine, Resinous, Spicy, Woody\n\nOriginating from the American Dwarf Hop Association, this experimental hop is a blend of Toyomidori and ADHA 94 hops. The latter, ADHA 94, is an intriguing combination of Summit and another experimental hop. ADHA-484 boasts a distinct aroma profile, characterized by prominent notes of cedar, wood, bubblegum, and spice. With an alpha acid content ranging from 10.5-12%, it's a versatile hop suitable for imparting both flavor and bitterness. Its cedar and spice nuances make it particularly well-suited for U.S. Pale Ales and American Saisons . Additionally, the unique combination of descriptors suggests that it might be an excellent choice for English beers or those that are oak-aged, offering a depth and complexity that can elevate the final brew."
