          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 8.4
          }
        },
        "notes": "Also known as: HBC 1019\n\nFlavor notes: Banana, Candy, Caramel, Coconut, Honeydew, Orange, Peach, Tropical Fruits\n\nDolcita, previously known as experimental hop HBC 1019, was developed by the Hop Breeding Company, a collaboration between John I. Haas and Yakima Chief Ranches. It is the product of a 2016 cross between two developmental varieties. This hop is not only agronomically advantageous, boasting high yields and an early harvest window, but it also presents a potent and pleasing mix of flavors. The flavor profile of Dolcita is reminiscent of a tropical and citrus fruit cocktail, which makes it an excellent choice for brewers looking to impart a bold, fruity, and complex character to their beers.\n\nThe aromatic qualities of Dolcita are impressive, with a spectrum that includes citrus, fruity and caramel notes. This hop variety is described as having a neo-mexicanus profile, which is known for its wild and vibrant flavors. The additional descriptors of peaches and cream, rhubarb and custard, piña colada, palm, and coconut shell suggest a hop that can contribute a distinctive and exotic touch to a brew. Dolcita imparts a bold and tropical character, making it suitable for IPAs, pale ales, or any beer style where a pronounced fruit-forward hop presence is desired."
      },
      {
        "name": "Dr. Rudi",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "New Zealand",
        "folder_path": "New Zealand",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
          "value": 11.0
        },
        "alpha_acid_range": {
          "minimum": {
            "unit": "%",
