          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 10.9
          }
        },
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Bergamot, Gooseberry, Lemon, Lilac, Lime, Mandarin, Pear, Pine, Pineapple, White Currant\n\nEXP 2/20 is a new addition to the brewing world, introduced by PolishHops. This experimental hop variety offers a complex and enticing medley of flavors and aromas, making it an exciting choice for homebrewers. Originating from Poland, EXP 2/20 combines traditional hop cultivation expertise with innovative breeding techniques, resulting in a hop that is both unique and versatile. Its diverse profile makes it suitable for a range of beer styles, allowing brewers to explore new and dynamic taste experiences.\n\nThe flavor profile of EXP 2/20 is truly remarkable, with a dominant citrus character complemented by a variety of other fruity notes. It features the bright, zesty flavors of lemon, bergamot, and mandarin, creating a lively and refreshing taste. Additionally, the presence of pineapple, pear, gooseberry, and white currant adds depth and complexity, offering brewers a rich palette to work with. These flavors make EXP 2/20 particularly well-suited for styles such as IPAs, pale ales, and other hop-forward beers where a vibrant citrus profile is desired."
      },
      {
        "name": "Falconer's Flight 7 C's",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "United States",
