      {
        "name": "HBC 353",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "United States",
        "folder_path": "United States",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
          "value": 7.0
        },
        "alpha_acid_range": {
          "minimum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 7.0
          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 9.0
          }
        },
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Chamomile, Elderflower, Floral, Grassy, Green Tea, Herbal, Honey, Nettle, Pleasant, Tarragon, Tea, Woody\n\nHBC 353 is a valuable addition to any homebrewer's arsenal, offering both bittering and aroma qualities. Originating from experimental breeding, this hop is akin to Willamette hops but boasts its own distinct character. The hop's aroma profile includes enticing notes of green tea, tarragon, elderflower, chamomile, and nettle, which contribute to a nuanced and aromatic brew. With its clean, low- to medium-hop flavor profile, HBC 353 is particularly well-suited for hot side additions in lager-like beers, making it a perfect fit for American Lager, Helles, Pilsner, Kolsch, Cream Ale, and Golden Ale styles, where it adds a noble-like quality and enhances drinkability."
      },
      {
        "name": "HBC 432",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "United States",
        "folder_path": "United States",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
          "value": 12.5
        },
        "alpha_acid_range": {
          "minimum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 11.4
          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 12.5
          }
        },
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Aromatic, Citrus, Fruity, Peach, Sweet, Tropical Fruits, Vibrant\n\nHBC 432, an intriguing experimental hop variety developed by the Hop Breeding Company, offers a delightful addition to the brewer's arsenal. While its exact origins may be shrouded in mystery, its flavor profile speaks volumes. With HBC 432, homebrewers can expect a burst of candied peach notes, adding a layer of sweetness and complexity to their creations. This unique characteristic makes it an excellent choice for brewers looking to infuse their beers with a fruity, almost confectionary essence. HBC 432 can elevate a wide range of styles, from pale ales to IPAs and beyond. Its flavors can harmonize beautifully with other fruit-forward hops or provide a standout feature in single-hop brews."
      },
      {
        "name": "HBC 472",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
