        },
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Aromatic, Banana, Cantaloupe, Cherry, Citrus, Herbal, Mango, Pineapple, Stone Fruit, Strawberry, Sweet, Tropical Fruits\n\nHBC 638 hops, a thrilling addition to the world of brewing, offer a captivating aroma profile reminiscent of a tropical paradise. Originating from the USA and developed by the Hop Breeding Company, a collaboration between John I. Haas and Yakima Chief Ranches, these experimental hops boast a delightful fusion of flavors. Homebrewers will find themselves enchanted by the tantalizing scents of mango, citrus, and sweet aromatic notes that HBC 638 imparts. Brewers experimenting with HBC 638 will discover a spectrum of possibilities in their creations. Whether seeking to enhance a traditional brew with a hint of citrus or aiming to craft a bold tropical-infused beer, these hops offer versatility and excitement."
      },
      {
