          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 6.1
          }
        },
        "substitutes": "Hallertauer Taurus, Warrior",
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Citrus, Fruity, Melon, Menthol, Orange, Pepper, Pine, Resinous, Spicy, Woody\n\nHerkules hops, also known as \"Hallertauer Herkules\", originated in Germany and are a product of the Hull Hop Research Institute, where they were developed as a high-alpha bittering hop in 2005. They are a cross between the Hallertauer Taurus and a male hop plant from the Hallertau region, which is renowned for its excellent hop varieties. The Herkules hops have quickly gained popularity among brewers for their impressive yield potential, high resistance to diseases, and exceptional bittering capabilities.\n\nThe flavor profile of Herkules hops is unique and robust, boasting a range of characteristics including spicy, herbal, and fruity notes. Often described as having flavors reminiscent of black pepper, fresh herbs, and tropical fruit, these hops are highly versatile and suitable for a wide range of beer styles. In beer brewing, Herkules hops are primarily used for their bittering properties, but their complex flavor profile also lends well to aroma additions. They work exceptionally well in German-style lagers, such as Pilsners and Bocks, but can also be used in Pale Ales, IPAs, and even Stouts, where their robust character can provide a delightful counterpoint to the malt-forward flavors. For homebrewers, Herkules hops are a great option to explore, offering an opportunity to create distinctive and flavorful beers that stand out from the crowd."
      },
      {
        "name": "Horizon",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "United States",
        "folder_path": "United States",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
          "value": 12.0
        },
        "alpha_acid_range": {
          "minimum": {
