        },
        "notes": "Also known as: AU 035\n\nFlavor notes: Citrus, Floral, Fruity, Herbal, Orange, Peach, Spicy, Tangy, White Pepper, Zesty\n\nHPA 035, also referred to as AU 035, was an experimental hop cultivated by Hop Products Australia (HPA). Originating from HPA farms in Australia, this hop variety was a subject of curiosity among brewers for its unique flavor profile. HPA 035 was characterized by prominent notes of orange and peach, which lent a refreshing and fruity dimension to beer recipes. Additionally, it boasted a dry spiciness reminiscent of white pepper, adding complexity to the overall taste profile. Unfortunately, despite its intriguing qualities, HPA 035 did not meet HPA's commercial expectations and has since been discontinued."
