          }
        },
        "substitutes": "Tettnanger",
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Anise, Aniseed, Chocolate, Citrus, Earthy, Grapefruit, Hay, Herbal, Lemon, Licorice, Tobacco\n\nMarynka hops, a product of Poland, are a dual-purpose variety known for their exceptional spiciness and unique flavor profile. The hops are a result of a cross between Brewer's Gold and a Yugoslavian male, and were officially registered in 1988. Marynka hops contain both good aroma values and pleasant bitterness properties, making them a versatile choice for brewers.\n\nThe flavor profile of Marynka hops is quite distinctive, featuring notes of hay, licorice, lemon, chocolate, and tobacco. These hops also exhibit a strong earthy and herbal aroma, with additional hints of grapefruit, citrus, aniseed, and hay. While Marynka hops are primarily used for bittering, they can also be used to provide a strong earthy, herbal aroma. This makes them a popular dual-purpose variety, suitable for use in all hop additions throughout the brewing process."
      },
      {
        "name": "Melba",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "Australia",
        "folder_path": "Australia",
