        },
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Citrus, Dank, Fruity, Guava, Juicy, Mango, Pineapple, Tangerine, Tropical Fruits, Watermelon\n\nU3/132 is a dual-purpose hop, which boasts an enticing blend of ripe mango, watermelon, pineapple, guava, tangerine peel, tropical punch, and a hint of dankness. It is not just about aroma but also brings a robust bittering potential to the brew. Originating from South Africa, this hop has a super high alpha acid content, typically accounting for around 18%. U3/132 can be a game-changer, especially for those looking to craft beers with a tropical twist. Its high alpha acid content means that it can be used both for bittering and aroma, making it a versatile choice for various beer styles. Whether you're brewing an IPA that bursts with tropical fruitiness or a pale ale with a subtle hint of tangerine peel, U3/132 can deliver that desired punch."
