      {
        "name": "Zagrava",
        "hop_type": "aroma/bittering",
        "origin": "Ukraine",
        "folder_path": "Ukraine",
        "alpha_acid": {
          "unit": "%",
          "value": 5.6
        },
        "alpha_acid_range": {
          "minimum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 4.1
          },
          "maximum": {
            "unit": "%",
            "value": 7.7
          }
        },
        "notes": "Flavor notes: Citrus, Earthy, Floral, Fresh, Fruity, Herbal, Pine, Spicy, Sweet, Woody\n\nZagrava hops, originating from Ukraine, represent a relatively new addition to the world of brewing, bringing with them a unique flavor profile that is both traditional and novel. The hop is known for its high essential oil content, which includes a significant amount of farnesene. This contributes to its aromatic properties, setting it apart from other varieties like Tradition and making it a closer relative to Spalter Select in terms of its sensory profile.\n\nThe flavor and aroma profile of Zagrava is described as spicy-floral, with a strong herbal backbone complemented by fruit notes. This makes it an excellent choice for brewers looking to create beers with a rich bouquet and a nuanced taste. Its characteristics are well-suited for lagers, where the subtle interplay of flavors can shine through. The hop's origin in Ukraine, a region with a significant history of hop production, adds a layer of depth to its story and appeal. Ukrainian hops, such as Zagrava, are protected by national rights and have been registered at the EU Community Plant Variety Office (CPVO), ensuring their unique qualities are preserved and recognized."
      },
