        "notes": "Flavor notes: Bright, Citrus, Crisp, Fresh, Juicy, Tangy, Vibrant, Zesty\n\nOriginating from the United States, Zoso hops are exclusive to Colorado, specifically cultivated at the Misty Mountain Hop Farm nestled in the Colorado Rocky Mountains. These hops are characterized as dual-purpose, boasting a high alpha acid content of around 10%. The flavor profile of Zoso is reminiscent of the popular Centennial hops but packs a more pronounced citrus punch, making it a standout choice for those desiring a citrus-forward brew. These strong citrus notes can complement a variety of beer styles, especially those that benefit from a bright and zesty character."
