        "mash_id": "Mash_24",
        "notes": "Barley's Homebrewing Supplies in New Westminster, BC provided this recipe as one of the official 2022 Canadian Homebrew Day recipes!\n\n\"This recipe is one of our most popular, but with a bit of a twist.\" – Barley's Homebrewing Supplies\n\nBarley's Tips\n • Abbey malt can also be used in place of the honey malt.\n • For yeast, any of the following should work: Escarpment Labs Cali Ale, Imperial Yeast A07 Flagship, Lallemand LalBrew BRY-97 West Coast Ale, Omega OYL-004 West Coast I, SafAle US-05, White Labs WLP001 California Ale, Wyeast WY1056.\n • OPTIONAL – add 21 g of loose earl grey tea (or 10 tea bags) for 7 minutes while the wort is chilling.\n\nBarley's is a homebrewing supply store in Metro Vancouver, BC, Canada.  They supply all of the equipment and ingredients for you to brew your own beer in the comfort of your own home.  If you can follow a recipe in the kitchen, you can homebrew!",
        "original_gravity": {
          "unit": "sg",
