        "notes": "Victor North of Niagara Brewing College provided this as one of the official 2021 Canadian Homebrew Day recipes!\n\n Victor says \"The village I live in was once called Temperanceville, and I like to name my recipes after local names and places.  I thought that it had a nice ring to it: the alliteration, and irony of naming a high ABV stout “Temperanceville”.  This recipe was picked from a recipe done four ways with three different yeasts and four different sugars to expedite the experimentation findings!\"",
