        "mash_id": "Mash_17",
        "notes": "Cory Day's award-winning kolsch was one of the official 2021 Canadian Homebrew Day recipes!\n\nCory says \"This is my recipe for one of my favourite kolsch.  Over the years it has won several medals and is a favourite of friends and family.  It was even served at my best friend's wedding – and the first keg to kick!  The beer is named after one of the running gags in one of my favourite movies, Step Brothers.  I hope everyone enjoys this and hits me up with a #PowCatalinaWineMixer on Twitter when they're taking a drink!\"\n\nCory's Tips\n • The softer the water the better! Target a ratio of 1 gypsum to 3 calcium chloride to a minimum of 50 ppm calcium\n • If you are using tap water, ensure you use metabisulfite or Campden tablets to neutralize chlorine and/or chloramines\n • Pitch lots of healthy yeast – two packs of Wyeast or White Labs, or one pack of Imperial Yeast and a 2-3 L starter\n • Don't substitute flaked wheat for the wheat malt!\n • If the recommended strains aren't available, other kolsch strains should work, including: Escarpment Labs Kolsch, Omega Yeast OYL-044 Kolsch II, Lallemand LalBrew Koln, Fermentis Safale K-97",
        "original_gravity": {
          "unit": "sg",
          "value": 1.04500
        },
        "final_gravity": {
          "unit": "sg",
          "value": 1.01125
        },
